hexdig (1.0.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New upstream release.
    - Add Mach-O parser (thin 32/64-bit, BE/LE) to identify Apple
      executables and shield embedded parsers from false-positive matches
      inside Mach-O binaries.
    - Fix segfaults and unbounded reads in the cramfs, dtb, tar, uimage
      and cpio parsers/extractors when file-controlled length or offset
      fields exceed the buffer.
    - Rewrite SquashFS parser to read v4 superblock fields at the correct
      offsets (block_size, s_major, bytes_used).
    - Tighten EXT4 superblock validation (first_data_block, per-group
      counts, inode/block ratio) to reject false positives in random
      binaries.
    - Locate 7-Zip on PATH using the per-platform candidate list so
      Debian's /usr/bin/7z is found even when the upstream `7zz` name is
      absent.

 -- Carmix <carmixdev@gmail.com>  Mon, 04 May 2026 09:21:49 +0200

